# Sensors for coding agents

This repo follows Martin Fowler's "Sensors for Coding Agents" approach: every architectural rule emits agent-readable self-correction guidance.

## Before editing

Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md). Both are kept in sync for Claude Code and Cursor.

## After editing

Local dev: Husky runs `lint-staged` on commit and `check:affected` on push.

**Cloud agents (no Husky):** before **every** `git commit`, run:

```bash
npm run precommit
git add -u
```

`precommit` = `format:affected` (write Prettier fixes) + `check:affected` (verify). CI runs `format:check` on the whole repo first — unformatted edits fail even when tests pass.

## Reading sensor output

- **Prettier**: `npm run format:check` in CI; scoped check in `check:affected`. Fix with `npm run format`.
- **verify:deps**: `npm run verify:deps`. Catches duplicate npm installs of override-pinned packages (notably `@a2ui/web_core` hoisted vs nested under `@a2ui/react`). After touching `@a2ui/*` or lockfiles, run this plus `npm run typecheck -w apps/web`.
- **ESLint**: messages come through a custom formatter at `packages/eslint-config/formatter.cjs`. A trailing "Agent guidance" section quotes the canonical fix per rule id. Read it before suppressing or raising a threshold.
- **dependency-cruiser**: `npm run verify:boundaries`. Each rule in `.dependency-cruiser.cjs` has a `comment` that doubles as the fix.
- **Modularity** (semantic, not automated): read [`docs/agents/modularity.md`](../../docs/agents/modularity.md). Cursor users consult [`.cursor/skills/modularity/review/SKILL.md`](../skills/modularity/review/SKILL.md) and apply the Balanced Coupling Model by hand.

## Suppressing a warning

The right move when a rule is wrong for your case. Format:

```
// eslint-disable-next-line <rule-id> -- (reason: <one-line why>)
```

The `-- (reason: ...)` syntax is enforced by reviewers; an unexplained disable is treated as an unresolved warning. For threshold rules on specific files, raise the threshold in a file-scoped `/* eslint <rule>: [...] */` block with the same reason syntax.

## Wire-change templates

When you touch an HTTP route, AG-UI event, MCP tool, or schema, see [`docs/recipes/`](../../docs/recipes/).
